{:id "add-readme"
 :title "Your first push"
 :level :basic
 :instructions
 "Clone this repository, create a README.md with something in it, commit it on main, and push. Leave welcome.txt alone — it was here before you."

 :setup
 {:commits [{:name    :seed
             :branch  "main"
             :author  :curator
             :when    [:hours-before 1]
             :message "Set up the workshop\n"
             :files   {"welcome.txt" "Welcome to l2git!\n"}}]}

 :steps
 [{:id :push-readme
   :hints
   ["It's the whole loop: get the repository, change it, record the change, send it back."
    "git clone <the url above>, create README.md with any text, then git add README.md, git commit -m \"Add README\", git push"
    "clone copies the entire repository — history and all — onto your machine. add stages your new file, commit records a snapshot of everything staged, and push sends your new commit back to the remote, where I'm watching for it."]
   :checks [{:cond [:branch-exists "main"]
             :fail "I don't see a main branch yet."}
            {:cond [:reachable :seed "main"]
             :fail "Your commits should build on the one that was already here — don't rewrite it away."}
            {:cond [:file-exists "main" "README.md"]
             :fail "The pushed commit doesn't contain a README.md."}
            {:cond [:file-nonblank "main" "README.md"]
             :fail "README.md is there, but it's empty — put something in it."}
            {:cond [:file-equals "main" "welcome.txt" "Welcome to l2git!\n"]
             :fail "welcome.txt was changed or removed — it should survive untouched."}]
   :pass "README.md received. That's a clone, a commit, and a push — the whole loop. Well done."}]}
